session-audit-attribute-dependency: auditExclusive/auditReset require audit

Classification: spec-deviation bug fix.

Specification (TPM 2.0 Part 2, Table "Definition of (UINT8) TPMA_SESSION
Bits"): "1 | auditExclusive | ... This setting is only allowed if the
*audit* attribute is SET (TPM_RC_ATTRIBUTES)." and "2 | auditReset | ...
This setting is only allowed if the *audit* attribute is SET
(TPM_RC_ATTRIBUTES)."

The reference ignores auditExclusive and auditReset on a non-password session
whose audit attribute is CLEAR (for a password session it already returns
TPM_RC_ATTRIBUTES), so it continues and fails later with another response
code (e.g. a later session's unmarshaling error, TPM_RC_SYMMETRIC or
TPM_RC_BAD_AUTH). The check is added to RetrieveSessionData() right after the
duplicate-handle check, i.e. before the decrypt/encrypt/audit checks, as in
tpm-rs. Found by differential fuzzing.
diff --git a/TPMCmd/tpm/src/main/SessionProcess.c b/TPMCmd/tpm/src/main/SessionProcess.c
--- a/TPMCmd/tpm/src/main/SessionProcess.c
+++ b/TPMCmd/tpm/src/main/SessionProcess.c
@@ -1280,6 +1280,13 @@
             if(s_sessionHandles[i] == s_sessionHandles[sessionIndex])
                 return TPM_RCS_HANDLE + errorIndex;
         }
+        // tpm-rs differential testing -- C-ref spec deviation fix (NOT determinism):
+        // auditExclusive and auditReset are "only allowed if the *audit* attribute
+        // is SET (TPM_RC_ATTRIBUTES)" (Part 2, TPMA_SESSION).
+        if((IS_ATTRIBUTE(sessionAttributes, TPMA_SESSION, auditExclusive)
+            || IS_ATTRIBUTE(sessionAttributes, TPMA_SESSION, auditReset))
+           && !IS_ATTRIBUTE(sessionAttributes, TPMA_SESSION, audit))
+            return TPM_RCS_ATTRIBUTES + errorIndex;
         // If the session is used for parameter encryption or audit as well, set
         // the corresponding Indexes.
 
